<h2>About the AI portfolio assistant</h2>
<p>The current assistant is an interactive local demo with authored, topic-matched answers. It does not call an LLM. Questions stay in this page’s memory. The latest question is carried in the address fragment when entering chat or switching languages. It is not sent to the server, but can remain in browser history or travel with a copied link; do not include private information. It cannot access the computer, private files, secrets, personal chat history, or location. Device time is used locally to select a greeting.</p>
<p>Only curated facts and explicitly listed source links are available to the guide. For anything outside those facts, it says it does not know. The site also supports an optional live mode, which is disabled until a server and provider are configured. If offered, it requires explicit opt-in before sending each question (without conversation history) to the site’s server and DeepSeek. A broad time-of-day category is sent for the greeting; no location is requested. A live model selects relevant facts and greeting wording from the reviewed public collection. The server validates the selected IDs and supplies the original wording and citation links; the model cannot invent new URLs or factual wording. Selection can still be mistaken. Provider retention policies apply, and visitors should not submit private information. The service does not log questions; its usage controls retain only aggregate request counts and short-lived hashed connection identifiers.</p>
